ort. The counter-argument is Axiom 1 read\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:613:3. **A `dao.jing.v2` that contains only the observer**, rather than a\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:619:   its own suite plus the `dao.space` and btree suites, which J1 runs.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:621:   the observer, including `transport-error`. A reviewer may prefer\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:622:   auto-adopting the gap cursor since materialization is idempotent; the plan\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:624:6. **`busy` on `request-*` while an envelope is unsent**, rather than queuing\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:6:# dao.jing on DaoStream v2 — the content-observer slice\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:10:(the storage-observer design) and [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md). Its\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:22:alternative. Neither blocks any phase. They are marked where they occur (J1,\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:25:## Context\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:30:observer walk (`jing.cljc:391`) and five sites in the file backend\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:38:One fact that shaped the revision: the v1 observer (`dao.jing/observer-state`,\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:43:## The problem, by piece\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:47:| `dao.jing/observer-state`, `observe-step!`               | `ds/next` on any v1 reader; inline `{:position 0}` cursors; bare `:ok`/`:blocked`/`:end`/`:daostream/gap`  | reader surface: `cursor`, `next`; opaque cursors; outcome maps            |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:51:| `dao.jing.mem`, `dao.jing.coordinate`, hashing, `materialize!`, `get`, `close!` | stream-free                                                                         | unchanged                                                                 |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:56:and `src/dev/psset_fixtures.clj` — **none for the observer**. `dao.space.index`\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:58:to the intake pool with v1 `ds/append!`. Seven test files call the v1 observer:\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:64:## Strategy\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:72:   of `dao.jing` is not: content addressing, `materialize!`, `get`, `close!`\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:76:   - `dao.jing` becomes the **stream-free core** in J1, by moving the v1\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:77:     observer out rather than by moving the core out (Decision 4, C2).\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:78:   - The v1 observer moves, unchanged, to **`dao.jing.observer`** (v1), and\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:80:   - The v2 observer is **`dao.jing.v2.observer`**, requiring `dao.jing` for\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:81:     `materialize!` and `dao.stream` for the reader surface.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:86:     coupling, not a port (Decision 2). Its consumers use only\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:88:2. **The content-observer slice, and nothing else.** One observer, one durable\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:89:   backend, one remote client with its handlers and a stepped materializer.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:94:No compatibility facade, alias, or dual protocol. The v1 observer and v1\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:97:## Decisions\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:101:### Decision 1 — The observer: entry shape, cursor discipline, gap\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:107:(observer/observer-state [{:stream h1 :cursor c1} {:stream h2 :cursor c2}])\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:111:`observer-state` no longer takes bare streams and fabricates `{:position 0}`.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:114:a resumed one — not the observer's. A member without a cursor, or whose stream\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:117:exception. `observer-state` accepts exactly the member shape it stores, so\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:118:`(observer-state (:members st))` rebuilds a pool from a previous state; that is\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:121:**Cursor discipline.** The observer retains exactly the successor `next`\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:122:returns, after `materialize!` succeeds, and never anything else. There is no\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:123:arithmetic on a cursor anywhere in `dao.jing.v2.observer`, and no test inspects\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:128:(observer/adopt-cursor state i cursor) ; cursor came from the stream: minted, successor, or gap recovery\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:139:| `:dao.stream/ok`                                         | a payload was materialized                                             | `:address`                          | successor     |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:150:acknowledged to their publisher, and never materialized. Materialization is\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:153:publisher will re-append. The observer must not answer it. `cursor-mismatch`\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:161:**Materialization failure is unchanged.** `materialize!` throwing propagates\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:172:names `dao.jing.observer` and the stream-free file backend (see Decision 2 for\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:173:the design-document change that entails); *Open items* — durable checkpoints\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:179:J4), *Resource lifecycle*, *Lineage*. Nothing semantic about DaoJing moves; the\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:180:migration changes how the observer reads, not what it is.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:182:### Decision 2 — `dao.jing.file`: the durable log was never a stream (option b)\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:185:detail. The migration removes the `dao.stream` coupling; it does not build a\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:190:stream.\" Decision 2 changes that description, and J4 rewrites it. That is a\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:222:acknowledges a put only after the log is flushed and `materialize!` returns the\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:227:observed later — which means redesigning `materialize!`'s acknowledgement and\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:239:question that **this plan does not create and no transport can cure**. J4\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:240:records it in `dao.jing.md`'s open items by name, **\"the content write path as\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:242:data, and `materialize!`'s return value would change. That redesign is **out of\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:244:`dao.space.index`, both of which call `materialize!` synchronously, and the\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:245:brief's boundary is `dao.jing*`. Decision 2 removes an unused internal\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:252:or create, truncate an incomplete tail, append a length-prefixed record and\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:258:stays readable, proven by a golden record **and** by the ported torn-tail\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:259:recovery cases (J1). The copy creates no second owner of the truncation logic\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:260:because J1 retires `dao.stream.log` in the same phase (N1).\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:263:first real consumer: durable observer checkpoints, or a `dao.space` local\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:272:### Decision 3 — `dao.jing.remote`: remote content needs a driver its caller owns\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:278:content handle. `jing/materialize!` and `jing/get` are local operations and\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:281:drives — plus a stepped materializer over it, because a remote client that can\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:282:put but cannot materialize is a raw adapter to a KV, not a DaoJing backend.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:285:and returns a verdict (`jing.cljc:277`); `materialize!` supplies the integrity\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:288:layering: J3a is the backend primitives, J3c is the materializer.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:301:duplication ends at J5.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:303:**Client side, J3a — backend primitives, stepped by the composition.**\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:309:(remote/step state budget)                     ; => {:state s' :completions [...] :diagnostics [...]}\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:318:  `allocator-error` (mints no id; its diagnostic is retained), and `terminal`.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:320:  `:dao.jing.v2.remote/busy` and allocate nothing, because `rpc/request!`\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:322:- **`step` is the only path that clears `busy`.** Its order is fixed:\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:333:  4. take completions and diagnostics exactly once.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:335:  A driver that only re-calls `request-*` can never clear a `busy`; it must\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:361:- **`:diagnostics`** is part of the step result and is published exactly once:\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:363:  diagnostics. A caller that discards them discards them knowingly.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:367:**Client side, J3c — the stepped materializer.**\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:370:(remote/request-materialize state payload)     ; => {:outcome k :state s' :id n?}\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:375:the id. On a `:inserted` completion, completes `{:id n :op :materialize\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:382:as data here. A `:lost` on either hop completes the materialization as\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:383:`:lost` with the reason. `busy` applies as for any request. The same per-id\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:385:Read-side hydration needs only J3a; `store-tree-async` depends on J3c.\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:396:\"async DaoJing backend\" that section waits for is not delivered by J3 alone —\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:400:### Decision 4 — Namespace layout and the end state, decided now\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:404:| `dao.jing`                | **in-place**: v1 observer moved out in J1; stream-free core            | none, direct or transitive                   | —                                                              |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:405:| `dao.jing.observer` (v1)  | **new in J1**: the v1 observer, unchanged code and `dao.stream` require | `dao.stream`                                 | seven test files until `dao.space`'s tests migrate             |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:406:| `dao.jing.v2.observer`    | **new** — the observer on v2                                           | none, direct or transitive                   | —                                                              |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:410:| `dao.jing.v2.remote`      | **new** — handlers, client primitives, materializer                    | none, direct or transitive                   | —                                                              |\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:414:**The end state, decided now, independent of `dao.stream`'s naming\ncollab/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:416:core), 