{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|''^####|P[0-9]|C[0-9]|N[0-9]|open item|abandon|diagnostic|tail|materializ|naming|retir'\"' docs/design/dao.jing.v2.implementation-plan.md\"","aggregated_output":"18:under C2 and N1) and collected in *Boundary of this plan*.\n20:## Context\n38:## The problem, by piece\n46:| `dao.jing.mem`, `dao.jing.coordinate`, hashing, `materialize!`, `get`, `close!` | stream-free                                                                         | unchanged                                                                 |\n59:## Strategy\n67:   of `dao.jing` is not: content addressing, `materialize!`, `get`, `close!`\n72:     observer out rather than by moving the core out (Decision 4, C2).\n76:     `materialize!` and `dao.stream` for the reader surface.\n84:   backend, one remote client with its handlers and a stepped materializer.\n92:## Decisions\n96:### Decision 1 — The observer: entry shape, cursor discipline, gap\n117:returns, after `materialize!` succeeds, and never anything else. There is no\n134:| `:dao.stream/ok`                                         | a payload was materialized                                             | `:address`                          | successor     |\n145:acknowledged to their publisher, and never materialized. Materialization is\n156:**Materialization failure is unchanged.** `materialize!` throwing propagates\n168:the design-document change that entails); *Open items* — durable checkpoints\n177:### Decision 2 — `dao.jing.file`: the durable log was never a stream (option b)\n180:detail. The migration removes the `dao.stream` coupling; it does not build a\n217:acknowledges a put only after the log is flushed and `materialize!` returns the\n222:observed later — which means redesigning `materialize!`'s acknowledgement and\n235:records it in `dao.jing.md`'s open items by name, **\"the content write path as\n237:data, and `materialize!`'s return value would change. That redesign is **out of\n239:`dao.space.index`, both of which call `materialize!` synchronously, and the\n247:or create, truncate an incomplete tail, append a length-prefixed record and\n253:stays readable, proven by a golden record **and** by the ported torn-tail\n255:because J1 retires `dao.stream.log` in the same phase (N1).\n267:### Decision 3 — `dao.jing.remote`: remote content needs a driver its caller owns\n273:content handle. `jing/materialize!` and `jing/get` are local operations and\n276:drives — plus a stepped materializer over it, because a remote client that can\n277:put but cannot materialize is a raw adapter to a KV, not a DaoJing backend.\n280:and returns a verdict (`jing.cljc:277`); `materialize!` supplies the integrity\n283:layering: J3a is the backend primitives, J3c is the materializer.\n304:(remote/step state budget)                     ; => {:state s' :completions [...] :diagnostics [...]}\n305:(remote/abandon state reason)                  ; => s'\n313:  `allocator-error` (mints no id; its diagnostic is retained), and `terminal`.\n325:     `rpc/abandon-unsent` with the terminal reason, so the never-accepted\n328:  4. take completions and diagnostics exactly once.\n334:- **`abandon state reason`** is the composition's tool for its own\n337:  which abandons before every rebind. It calls `rpc/abandon-unsent`; the\n338:  completion carries `:dao.stream.rpc/abandoned` when no terminal reason\n353:  outcome, and `:dao.stream.rpc/abandoned` are examples, not a closed\n356:- **`:diagnostics`** is part of the step result and is published exactly once:\n358:  diagnostics. A caller that discards them discards them knowingly.\n362:**Client side, J3c — the stepped materializer.**\n365:(remote/request-materialize state payload)     ; => {:outcome k :state s' :id n?}\n370:the id. On a `:inserted` completion, completes `{:id n :op :materialize\n377:as data here. A `:lost` on either hop completes the materialization as\n395:### Decision 4 — Namespace layout and the end state, decided now\n405:| `dao.jing.v2.remote`      | **new** — handlers, client primitives, materializer                    | none, direct or transitive                   | —                                                              |\n409:**The end state, decided now, independent of `dao.stream`'s naming\n412:primitives, materializer). The `.v2.` segment is the transient marker and\n415:`dao.jing.v2.*` namespaces into those slots. This follows from the C2 remedy:\n434:spelling, and `:cljd` in tail position silently fails. Full cljd namespace\n437:## Divergence register\n450:| `jing/materialize!` over a remote handle                                                         | `request-materialize`: derive, put, verify on `:present`, complete with the address                  | the integrity behavior of `jing.cljc:276-293` must survive the loss of the handle                     |\n462:`torn-tail-test` is ported, as recovery evidence); `remote_test`'s\n468:## Phase J0 — What exists\n475:  `take-diagnostics`, `unsent?`, `abandon-unsent`, `rebind`),\n484:  `test/dao/stream/log_test.cljc:100-135` (`torn-tail-test`) for J1;\n488:## Phase J1 — `dao.jing` stream-free; `dao.jing.file` without a stream\n490:Three deliverables in one phase, because the second and third retire the same\n518:  tail exactly as `dao.stream.log/make-log-stream` does: a tail shorter than\n527:  `[address payload]` vector of a file, for tests and diagnostics; it opens,\n531:- **Torn-tail recovery tests, ported from `log_test.cljc:100-135` on all three\n534:  closed on it before reaching the torn tail. The ported test therefore:\n539:  subsequent `materialize!` lands clean and survives reopen. A second case\n540:  hand-writes a sub-four-byte tail (two bytes) and asserts the same. A third\n553:into the ambient registry v2 retires, and leaving it would make the copied\n555:until wholesale v1 deletion. `dao.stream.file` (`:file`, live-tail, consumed\n562:here, so per-transport retirement at the last consumer's migration is the\n565:stream-plan-owned dependency named **\"legacy append-log retirement\"**,\n578:## Phase J2 — `dao.jing.v2.observer`\n593:  interleave, cursor advances only after successful materialization. Cursor\n599:  materializes the live value.\n613:## Phase J3 — `dao.jing.v2.remote`\n617:`request-put`, `request-get`, `step`, `abandon`, per *Decision 3*. Tests,\n637:- **`abandon`** before an explicit rebind completes the unsent request with\n638:  `:dao.stream.rpc/abandoned`; ids remain monotonic.\n643:  outcome, mints no id, and its diagnostic appears in the next `step`'s\n644:  `:diagnostics`.\n647:  `:diagnostics`.\n650:  its documented reason set — has a branch; completions and diagnostics\n667:with the same deposit cursor resumed; a descriptor naming a path nothing\n670:**J3c — the stepped materializer.** `request-materialize` per *Decision 3*,\n681:- `:lost` on the verify hop completes the materialization as `:lost` with the\n690:## Phase J4 — Design prose\n699:  materializer the composition drives, and states that `jing/materialize!`\n706:  such a function, and `materialize!` returns its address synchronously after\n710:  arrives later as data, and `materialize!`'s return value changes — reaching\n719:## Phase J5 — Deletion and the naming decision, executed\n737:## Host matrix\n741:| J1    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | three host branches in `dao.jing.file`, `:cljd` first; torn-tail fixtures hand-written per host as in `log_test.cljc` |\n753:## Invariants, checked\n770:## Boundary of this plan\n784:  (J1.3); alternative: stream-plan-owned \"legacy append-log retirement\",\n789:driven state machine with a stepped materializer, not a handle (Decision 3);\n818:  explicit materialization acknowledgement; garbage collection — the open\n825:## End condition\n832:  gone, or its retirement is a named, atomically coordinated stream-plan\n838:- `dao.jing.v2.remote` round-trips put, get and **materialize** through\n841:  `step`; completes every lost, abandoned and unsent-at-terminal request as\n842:  data exactly once; and publishes diagnostics exactly once.\n844:  driven remote client with its materializer, and records the write-path\n845:  question as an open item.\n857:## What changed from the round-1 draft, and why\n859:- **A1 / C5 — `step` ordering and abandonment.** Round 1 specified a `busy`\n863:  carried silently across `rebind`. `step` now re-attempts, polls, abandons on\n864:  terminal, then publishes; `abandon` is exposed; both cases are tested.\n866:- **A2 — `:diagnostics` in the step result**, published exactly once; round 1\n868:- **A3 / N1 — torn-tail coverage and the orphaned transport.** Round 1's\n871:  J1 now ports `torn-tail-test` with the fixture adaptation (a valid Jing\n873:  negative-length cases, and retires `dao.stream.log` in the same phase so\n876:- **C1 — Decision 2 stands, with two concessions.** It now states that it\n879:  synchronous content handle as an open item that no transport cures; and\n882:- **C2 / C4 — the observer moves out; the end state is decided.** The fact\n886:  three namespaces, decided now, independent of `dao.stream`'s naming.\n889:- **C3 — the materializer.** Round 1's `request-put` was the backend primitive\n891:  verification. J3a keeps the primitives, J3c adds `request-materialize`, the\n894:- **C6 — completion totality by construction**: reason pass-through,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
