{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '760,900p' docs/design/dao.jing.v2.implementation-plan.md | nl -ba -v760\"","aggregated_output":"   760\t  composition calls again. Nothing self-schedules.\n   761\t- **No callbacks.** None in any new public surface. The ws adapter map is the\n   762\t  transport's, confined to J3b's composition.\n   763\t- **No shared mutable state.** A content handle is owned by whoever created\n   764\t  it; the RPC state is a value threaded by one driver.\n   765\t- **Interpretation and execution stay separate.** The observer interprets the\n   766\t  pool; the backend executes the write; the remote client interprets\n   767\t  completions; the serving composition executes the socket.\n   768\t- **No assumed graphs.** Nothing here relates content addresses to each other.\n   769\t\n   770\t## Boundary of this plan\n   771\t\n   772\t**Untouched:** `dao.jing.mem`; v1 `dao.jing.remote` until J5;\n   773\t`dao.jing.coordinate`; `dao.jing.dht`, `dao.jing.dht.kad`, `dao.jing.dht.node`;\n   774\tevery `dao.space*` and `dao.data.btree*` `src/` namespace; `dao.stream` v1 in\n   775\tevery form except `dao.stream.log`.\n   776\t\n   777\t**Touched outside `dao.jing*`, both scope-contingent, both decided at\n   778\tauthorization:**\n   779\t\n   780\t- five `test/dao/space/` files, one require line and alias each (J1.1);\n   781\t  alternative: the documentation route, with transitive v1 stated as an\n   782\t  end-condition bullet until J5.\n   783\t- `src/cljc/dao/stream/log.cljc` and `test/dao/stream/log_test.cljc`, deleted\n   784\t  (J1.3); alternative: stream-plan-owned \"legacy append-log retirement\",\n   785\t  coordinated atomically with J1.\n   786\t\n   787\t**Architectural decisions**, made here: the durable log is not a stream and\n   788\tthe write-path redesign is a separate item (Decision 2); remote content is a\n   789\tdriven state machine with a stepped materializer, not a handle (Decision 3);\n   790\tthe observer's cursor and non-progress discipline (Decision 1); the\n   791\tthree-namespace end state and the observer move-out (Decision 4).\n   792\t\n   793\t**Implementation gaps**, left open knowingly: the v2 remote client has no\n   794\tcoordinate and cannot be reached from `dao.jing.coordinate/open!`; the\n   795\tserving side exists only as test compositions; the promise-shaped\n   796\t`hydrate-async`/`store-tree-async` of `dao.data.btree.md` §5.4 is a driver\n   797\tover this client that this plan does not build.\n   798\t\n   799\t**Intentionally deferred**, each to a named home:\n   800\t\n   801\t- **The content write path as an effect stream** — a DaoJing architecture\n   802\t  item recorded in J4; it reaches `dao.data.btree.storage` and\n   803\t  `dao.space.index` and is not a migration.\n   804\t- `dao.jing.dht` and `dao.jing.dht.node` — UDP transport, deferred by the\n   805\t  stream plan; `dht.cljc` itself requires no `dao.stream`, and `node.cljc`'s\n   806\t  `dao.stream.transit` require goes with the UDP transport's own migration.\n   807\t- `dao.space`'s own migration: `publish-index!`'s v1 `ds/append!` into the\n   808\t  intake pool, `snapshot-datoms`' `{:position 0}` walk, the published-index\n   809\t  `defopen`, `DaoStreamLog`'s writer face, and switching its tests from\n   810\t  `dao.jing.observer` (v1) to the v2 observer.\n   811\t- The `:dao.jing/remote` coordinate under v2 and the async hydration driver\n   812\t  (`dao.data.btree.md` §5.4) — `dao.space`'s query-side plan; read hydration\n   813\t  needs J3a, `store-tree-async` needs J3c.\n   814\t- A content-serving endpoint as production infrastructure — the composition\n   815\t  that starts, serves and stops a content server belongs to whatever product\n   816\t  surface needs it, as the REPL's R4 did for the REPL.\n   817\t- Canonical encoding; durable observer checkpoints and a long-running runner;\n   818\t  explicit materialization acknowledgement; garbage collection — the open\n   819\t  items of `dao.jing.md`, unchanged. Checkpoints gain only the shape\n   820\t  constraint that the persisted value is the transport's own cursor, whose\n   821\t  serializability the contract leaves TBD.\n   822\t- A v2 file or append-log transport — until a consumer needs cursors over a\n   823\t  durable file.\n   824\t\n   825\t## End condition\n   826\t\n   827\tComplete when all of the following hold on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd:\n   828\t\n   829\t- `dao.jing` requires no `dao.stream*` namespace. `dao.jing.file` requires no\n   830\t  `dao.stream*` namespace, reads every content file v1 wrote including a\n   831\t  torn one, and its suite runs with no stream fixture. `dao.stream.log` is\n   832\t  gone, or its retirement is a named, atomically coordinated stream-plan\n   833\t  dependency landed with J1.\n   834\t- `dao.jing.v2.observer` observes v2 reader handles with stream-minted\n   835\t  cursors, is total over `dao.stream/outcomes-next` by a\n   836\t  declaration-driven test, retains only successors and adopted cursors, and\n   837\t  requires only `dao.jing` and `dao.stream`.\n   838\t- `dao.jing.v2.remote` round-trips put, get and **materialize** through\n   839\t  `dao.stream.apply` and `dao.stream.rpc` over ring buffers on all three\n   840\t  hosts and over `dao.stream.ws` on each; clears `busy` only through\n   841\t  `step`; completes every lost, abandoned and unsent-at-terminal request as\n   842\t  data exactly once; and publishes diagnostics exactly once.\n   843\t- `dao.jing.md` describes the v2 observer, the stream-free file backend, the\n   844\t  driven remote client with its materializer, and records the write-path\n   845\t  question as an open item.\n   846\t- No namespace under `dao.jing.v2*` requires `dao.stream` or\n   847\t  `dao.stream.rpc.*`, **directly or transitively** — or, under the\n   848\t  documentation route, `dao.jing.v2*` is transitively v1 until J5, stated as\n   849\t  this bullet.\n   850\t- Once `dao.space` has migrated: v1 `dao.jing.observer` and v1\n   851\t  `dao.jing.remote` are deleted, and `dao.jing.v2.observer` and\n   852\t  `dao.jing.v2.remote` are renamed to `dao.jing.observer` and\n   853\t  `dao.jing.remote`.\n   854\t\n   855\t---\n   856\t\n   857\t## What changed from the round-1 draft, and why\n   858\t\n   859\t- **A1 / C5 — `step` ordering and abandonment.** Round 1 specified a `busy`\n   860\t  guard and a `step` that only polled; since `rpc/request!` is the sole path\n   861\t  that re-attempts an unsent envelope and `lose-outstanding` covers\n   862\t  `:outstanding` only, `busy` could never clear and an unsent request was\n   863\t  carried silently across `rebind`. `step` now re-attempts, polls, abandons on\n   864\t  terminal, then publishes; `abandon` is exposed; both cases are tested.\n   865\t  Cause: reasoning from the sibling plans' prose instead of `rpc.cljc`.\n   866\t- **A2 — `:diagnostics` in the step result**, published exactly once; round 1\n   867\t  claimed to take them and had nowhere to put them.\n   868\t- **A3 / N1 — torn-tail coverage and the orphaned transport.** Round 1's\n   869\t  golden record proved clean replay only while copying the truncation loops\n   870\t  out of `dao.stream.log`; the only recovery test would have died with v1.\n   871\t  J1 now ports `torn-tail-test` with the fixture adaptation (a valid Jing\n   872\t  record first, since `[11 22]` is not decodable) plus sub-four-byte and\n   873\t  negative-length cases, and retires `dao.stream.log` in the same phase so\n   874\t  the framing has one owner. Scope-contingent, with the atomic stream-plan\n   875\t  alternative named and \"leave it standing\" excluded.\n   876\t- **C1 — Decision 2 stands, with two concessions.** It now states that it\n   877\t  amends `dao.jing.md`'s own description of the file backend, routed as a\n   878\t  design change; records the pre-existing Host-Boundaries question about the\n   879\t  synchronous content handle as an open item that no transport cures; and\n   880\t  explains via the no-wait rule why option (a) is the write-path redesign in\n   881\t  disguise rather than a like-for-like transport.\n   882\t- **C2 / C4 — the observer moves out; the end state is decided.** The fact\n   883\t  that the v1 observer has no `src/` caller made \"move the observer out\"\n   884\t  cheaper than \"extract the core\" by nine production namespaces. `dao.jing`\n   885\t  is stream-free from J1; the transitive gate is literal; the end state is\n   886\t  three namespaces, decided now, independent of `dao.stream`'s naming.\n   887\t  Seven test repoints, not five; five are scope-contingent with the\n   888\t  documentation route named.\n   889\t- **C3 — the materializer.** Round 1's `request-put` was the backend primitive\n   890\t  and was called a DaoJing backend; it omitted derivation and read-back\n   891\t  verification. J3a keeps the primitives, J3c adds `request-materialize`, the\n   892\t  end condition includes it, and the §5.4 claim is narrowed to \"a driver over\n   893\t  this client, not built here\".\n   894\t- **C6 — completion totality by construction**: reason pass-through,\n   895\t  `allocator-error` in the request outcome set, declaration-driven test.\n   896\t- **Line reference fix:** `jing_test.cljc` observer section is lines 322–560.\n   897\t- **Not changed:** Decision 1 in substance, the in-place rewrite of\n   898\t  `dao.jing.file`, the deferral of the `:dao.jing/remote` coordinate to\n   899\t  `dao.space`'s plan, and the phase ordering J1 → J2 → J3 → J4 → J5. Both\n   900\t  reviews and both consensus seats found these sound.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
