{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '578,690p' docs/design/dao.jing.v2.implementation-plan.md | nl -ba -v578\"","aggregated_output":"   578\t## Phase J2 — `dao.jing.v2.observer`\n   579\t\n   580\t`src/cljc/dao/jing/v2/observer.cljc`: `observer-state`, `observe-step!`,\n   581\t`adopt-cursor`, per *Decision 1*. Requires `dao.jing` and `dao.stream`\n   582\tonly, and after J1 `dao.jing` requires no `dao.stream`, so the namespace is\n   583\tv1-free directly and transitively.\n   584\t\n   585\tTests, `test/dao/jing/v2/observer_test.cljc`, over v2 ring buffers created\n   586\twith `ringbuffer/create!` and cursors minted with\n   587\t`stream/cursor … :dao.stream/oldest`:\n   588\t\n   589\t- every observer case from the former `jing_test.cljc` lines 322–560, ported:\n   590\t  plain-data state, empty pool blocked, all blocked, hashing and retrieval,\n   591\t  equal payloads from two streams converge, blocked/ended members do not\n   592\t  starve others, all ended, drains then end, fair round-robin, strict\n   593\t  interleave, cursor advances only after successful materialization. Cursor\n   594\t  assertions become successor-equality assertions, never position arithmetic.\n   595\t- **gap**: a capacity-2 ring buffer with three appends; the signal is\n   596\t  `:dao.stream/gap` with `:member 0` and a `:cursor`; the member cursor is\n   597\t  unchanged; the other member still progresses; the gap reports again on the\n   598\t  next turn; after `adopt-cursor` with the recovery cursor the member\n   599\t  materializes the live value.\n   600\t- **defect outcomes**: a reified reader handle scripted to answer\n   601\t  `cursor-mismatch`, `invalid-cursor`, `transport-error` (and, for the\n   602\t  totality test, each outcome in `dao.stream/outcomes-next`); assert the\n   603\t  signal, `:member`, `:result`, unchanged cursor, and that an outcome outside\n   604\t  the declared set throws.\n   605\t- **members round-trip**: `(observer-state (remove-nth (:members st) i))`\n   606\t  keeps the remaining members' cursors.\n   607\t- `observer-convergence-test` from `file_test`, over the J1 file backend.\n   608\t\n   609\tDeliverable: `dao.jing.v2.observer` on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd; `Testing\n   610\tdao.jing.v2.observer-test` confirmed in the Node output; no namespace under\n   611\t`dao.jing.v2*` requires `dao.stream` **directly or transitively**.\n   612\t\n   613\t## Phase J3 — `dao.jing.v2.remote`\n   614\t\n   615\t**J3a — backend primitives, socket-free, all three hosts.**\n   616\t`src/cljc/dao/jing/v2/remote.cljc`: `default-handlers`, `client-state`,\n   617\t`request-put`, `request-get`, `step`, `abandon`, per *Decision 3*. Tests,\n   618\t`test/dao/jing/v2/remote_test.cljc`, mirror `rpc_test.cljc`: request and\n   619\tresponse media are two ring buffers; the server side is `apply/server-state`\n   620\t+ `apply/serve-once!` over `default-handlers` on a `dao.jing.mem` store; the\n   621\tclient is `rpc/client-state` over the same media, wrapped by `client-state`.\n   622\t\n   623\t- put then get round-trips through `step`; duplicate put completes `:present`;\n   624\t  absent get completes `:found? false`; a stored `nil` and a stored\n   625\t  `{:found? true :value \"hello\"}` round-trip exactly.\n   626\t- `request-*` on a non-segment address throws before allocation; a handler\n   627\t  rejecting a hash-mismatched address completes as `:error`.\n   628\t- **`busy` clears only through `step`**: a scripted writer answering `full`\n   629\t  once: `pending-request`; a second request returns `busy` and allocates\n   630\t  nothing; `step` re-attempts and its result carries `requested`; exactly one\n   631\t  id allocated; then a case where the driver only re-calls `request-*` and\n   632\t  asserts `busy` persists.\n   633\t- **unsent at detach**: a request left `pending-request`, then `/detached`\n   634\t  deposited on the response medium; `step` produces exactly one `:lost`\n   635\t  completion for it with `/detached` as the reason, and `:unsent` is empty in\n   636\t  the returned state; after `rebind` the old envelope is never sent.\n   637\t- **`abandon`** before an explicit rebind completes the unsent request with\n   638\t  `:dao.stream.rpc/abandoned`; ids remain monotonic.\n   639\t- gap on the response medium completes every outstanding request as `:lost`\n   640\t  with `:dao.stream/gap`; reader `cursor-mismatch`, `invalid-cursor` and\n   641\t  `end` complete as `:lost` with those exact keywords.\n   642\t- `allocator-error` on an exhausted or colliding allocator returns that\n   643\t  outcome, mints no id, and its diagnostic appears in the next `step`'s\n   644\t  `:diagnostics`.\n   645\t- malformed responses complete as `:error` with the malformed-response code\n   646\t  and never as `:found?`; unsolicited responses and decode errors appear in\n   647\t  `:diagnostics`.\n   648\t- **declaration-driven totality**: every keyword `dao.stream.rpc` can emit\n   649\t  as an outcome or reason — enumerated from that namespace's public vars and\n   650\t  its documented reason set — has a branch; completions and diagnostics\n   651\t  publish exactly once and are empty in the state returned after `step`.\n   652\t- `default-handlers` on a handle without `:put-content-fn` throws at\n   653\t  construction.\n   654\t\n   655\t**J3b — over `dao.stream.ws`, same process, all three hosts.** A serving\n   656\tcomposition assembled in the test from `dao.stream.serving` and the host\n   657\t`connect!`/`bind!` seams, exactly as `test/dao/stream/ws_test.cljc` and\n   658\t`serving_test.cljc` do; the served stream is a capacity-1 identity anchor as\n   659\tthe REPL's D3 settled. The client mints its `:dao.stream/newest` cursor on\n   660\tits traffic medium *before* `attach!`, builds the RPC state with\n   661\t`rpc.ws/init-client` from the whole `attach!` result, and wraps it with\n   662\t`client-state`. Prove: put and get round-trip over the wire; two clients see\n   663\teach other's writes; the file backend survives a stop, restart and reattach;\n   664\tkilling the connection completes an *accepted* outstanding request as `:lost`\n   665\twith `/detached`, and **a kill with an unsent request** produces exactly one\n   666\t`:lost` completion and an empty `:unsent` after `rebind` on a fresh `attach!`,\n   667\twith the same deposit cursor resumed; a descriptor naming a path nothing\n   668\tserves completes as `:lost` with `/not-found`.\n   669\t\n   670\t**J3c — the stepped materializer.** `request-materialize` per *Decision 3*,\n   671\tover the J3a primitives, in the same namespace. Tests, socket-free, on all\n   672\tthree hosts:\n   673\t\n   674\t- fresh payload: one put, completes `:inserted` with the derived address.\n   675\t- present payload: put answers `:present`, a second correlated get is issued,\n   676\t  equality holds, completes `:present` with the address; exactly two ids.\n   677\t- present but the server's get returns `:found? false`: completes `:error`\n   678\t  with `/present-but-absent`.\n   679\t- present but unequal (a scripted server store seeded with a different value\n   680\t  at the same address): completes `:error` with `/integrity-failure`.\n   681\t- `:lost` on the verify hop completes the materialization as `:lost` with the\n   682\t  reason; a caller's own `request-get` for the same address during a verify\n   683\t  hop is not confused with it (per-id record).\n   684\t- `busy` during the verify hop behaves as for any request.\n   685\t\n   686\tDeliverable: J3a and J3c green on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd; J3b green on clj\n   687\tand cljs (Node), and on cljd through the cljd ws lane. The cljd test\n   688\tregenerates `test/cljd-out/`; one process owns it at a time.\n   689\t\n   690\t## Phase J4 — Design prose\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
